        <mxCell id="er_t" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=17;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1f2430" value="Entity relationships" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="600" x="-420" y="-320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="er_ts" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#6b7280" value="The eleven Firestore collections and the joins between them. Crow&#39;s foot: a bar is one, a fork is many, a circle is optional. &lt;b&gt;The human id is the document id&lt;/b&gt; wherever one exists (b216, R-216-301, EQ-216-01, FD-216-14, REQ-4192) — every cross-reference already holds that string; logBook and equipmentHistory take auto-ids. A filled diamond is an embedded array: it lives inside the document, not in a collection of its own." vertex="1">
