        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="er_nLog" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff8e6;strokeColor=#b8860b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11" value="&lt;b&gt;One audit trail, read three ways.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr size=&#39;1&#39;&gt;The Log Book and Historical Records are the same collection behind different filters — an audit trail with two sources is one that can disagree with itself. isEstateRecord() holds personnel entries back (Office Staff reach Records and not the Log Book); isSignificant() is what Records shows by default — anything carrying a &lt;i&gt;reason&lt;/i&gt;, every alarm, anything refused, withdrawn, deleted or archived; isRoutineReading() is what the Log Book&#39;s &lt;i&gt;Actions only&lt;/i&gt; toggle hides. Measured once, routine crossings were 82% of the collection." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="210" width="390" x="-880" y="570" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="er_nId" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff8e6;strokeColor=#b8860b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11" value="&lt;b&gt;No join table anywhere.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr size=&#39;1&#39;&gt;Every query is single-collection and single-field-ordered, so firestore.indexes.json stays empty. A foreign key is resolved in the client, against the one list app-state already holds — which is why the sidebar badge and the dashboard tile cannot disagree." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="390" x="-880" y="800" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="er_nInv" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fillColor=#fff8e6;strokeColor=#b8860b;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11" value="&lt;b&gt;Invariants the code relies on&lt;/b&gt;&lt;hr size=&#39;1&#39;&gt;· Equipment counts: running + faulty + underMaintenance = quantity.&lt;br&gt;· A fire detector is &lt;b&gt;two records&lt;/b&gt; — an equipmentUnit (the asset) and a sensor (the live state) — joined by linkedEquipmentId, never merged.&lt;br&gt;· Equipment and sensor &lt;i&gt;types&lt;/i&gt; are data-driven registries, not hardcoded unions.&lt;br&gt;· A status is never a free string: it must be a statuses[].id on the sensor&#39;s own type." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="480" x="890" y="920" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
